  "label": "User projected onto the cat as 'everyone else at Auschwitz'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the cat, which is anthropomorphized and used as a stand-in for 'everyone else at Auschwitz' in the meme's text. The user identifies with the cat's position in the scene, imagining themselves as the one performing the mundane action (pulling pizza out of the oven) while others are suffering in Auschwitz. This projection is implicit, not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but is inferred from the meme's structure where the cat represents the user's imagined self in the absurd, darkly humorous scenario.",
